## 17. Acceptance Criteria 

The MVP is considered ready when: 

- Shopkeeper can install PrintHub using one Windows installer. 
- Shopkeeper can register using only shop name and mobile number. 
- Application runs its local server in the background. 
- Application discovers installed printers. 
- Shopkeeper can configure printer roles and pricing. 
- Shopkeeper can configure UPI details. 
- Application generates a QR code using the shop's mobile number. 
- Customer can open the shop-specific page. 
- Customer can upload multiple documents. 
- Customer can reorder and remove documents. 
- Customer can preview A4 output. 
- Customer can configure supported print options. 
- Customer cannot select physical printers or driver settings. 
- Customer can calculate the final price. 
- Customer can initiate UPI payment. 
- Shopkeeper can manually verify payment. 
- Verified jobs are automatically sent to the appropriate printer. 
- Multiple customers can submit jobs concurrently. 
- Multiple printers can process independent queues. 
- Jobs survive application restarts. 
- Successfully printed documents are deleted. 
- Failed and uncertain jobs remain recoverable. 
- Each shop's data remains isolated in its own installation. 
- No cloud backend or central database is required for the MVP. 

## 18. Out of Scope for MVP 

- Central cloud backend. 
- Central multi-tenant database. 
- Cloud document storage. 
- Payment gateway integration. 
- Automatic bank or UPI payment verification. 
- Remote printing over the public internet. 
- Customer accounts and registration. 
- Shop addresses and business profiles. 
- Mobile applications. 
- DOCX and advanced office document support. 
- Remote shop monitoring. 
- Centralized analytics. 

--- 

## Final Architecture Principle 

**One shop = One Windows installation = One local backend = One local database = One independent printing environment.** 

All shops share the same static customer frontend, but each shop's Windows application handles its own configuration, customers, files, payment confirmation, queues and printers. 

The mobile number identifies the shop in the customer URL. It does not create a central tenant database. 

The MVP should prioritize reliable local connectivity, printer compatibility, safe job execution and document cleanup over adding unnecessary cloud infrastructure.
